'''''Pelargonium grandiflorum''''' is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Geraniaceae]], native to the southwestern [[Cape Provinces]] of South Africa.<ref name="POWO_376255-1" >{{cite POWO |id=376255-1 |title=''Pelargonium grandiflorum'' Willd. |access-date=4 January 2023 }}</ref> It may be a parent of the cultivated ''[[Pelargonium × domesticum]]'' (regal pelargonium) with ''[[Pelargonium cucullatum]]''.<ref name="POWO_376059-1" >{{cite POWO |id=376059-1 |title=''Pelargonium'' × ''domesticum'' L.H.Bailey |access-date=4 January 2023 }}</ref><ref>{{cite journal |title=History and Culture of Regal Pelargonium |date=January 2001 |last1=Loehrlein |first1=Marietta M. |last2=Craig |first2=Richard |journal=HortTechnology |volume=11 |issue=2 |pages=289–296 |doi=10.21273/HORTTECH.11.2.289 |doi-access=free }}</ref>

